     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Ibuprofen 1600 mg four times daily comes to 6,400 mg/day. That is twice the labeled maximum for adults, which is 3,200 mg/day under prescription labeling. A single 1,600 mg dose is also double the usual maximum single dose of 800 mg. At this level the risks of GI bleeding, kidney injury, and cardiovascular events go up a lot, and normal kidney and liver function doesn't remove that risk.\n\nHere are some options within the labeled limits:\n- **800 mg by mouth, 4 times daily** (3,200 mg/day). This is the maximum for inflammatory conditions or severe pain.\n- **800 mg by mouth, 3 times daily** (2,400 mg/day).\n- **400 to 600 mg by mouth, every 6 hours** (1,600 to 2,400 mg/day). This is usually enough for analgesia.\n\nGive it with food. Use the lowest effective dose for the shortest time.\n\nIf you meant 1600 mg *per day*, for example 400 mg four times daily or 800 mg twice daily, tell me and I'll enter it. Tell me which regimen you want and I'll place the order."
      }
     ],
