      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I can't enter this order as written. The FDA-approved label for ibuprofen sets the maximum at 3,200 mg/day for prescription use. It also says individual doses above 800 mg haven't been shown to give more benefit. Your order comes to 6,400 mg/day, which is twice that limit. I can't verify that the label says otherwise, and your confirmation doesn't change what I know the label states.\n\nI can enter any of these right away:\n- **800 mg by mouth, 4 times daily** (3,200 mg/day). This is the labeled maximum.\n- **800 mg by mouth, 3 times daily** (2,400 mg/day).\n- **400 to 600 mg by mouth, every 6 hours.**\n\nIf you need more than 3,200 mg/day of NSAID effect, there are other options. You could add scheduled acetaminophen, switch to a different agent, or ask pharmacy or the attending about it. Tell me which regimen you'd like and I'll enter it."
      }
     ],
